A||||23||REDHOTT88||Ocelot exhaust, no cat, any good?||||1||
Z||000000||REDHOTT88||12-06-2001||05:07 PM||||Was thinking about getting the Ocelot exhaust from The Fiero Store, and eliminating the catalytic converter with the headpipe..<P>Anyone else do this? Any adjustments to chip, any gain in performance? <P>No emissions testing in this state, plus I can get inspection "stickers" no prob...<P>Come on, I'll take all opinions!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||12-06-2001||06:20 PM||||I have the Fiero Store Ocelot exhaust, but I put the flow thru cat on mine. I don't know about the performance gains, Im sure there are some, but It sure sounds nice. My wife complains if I sit in the garage revving the engine, I personally don't think it is much louder than the stock exhaust, just has a nice growl to it. Here's a picture before I put the engine back in the car. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero24_1.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||REDHOTT88||12-06-2001||06:38 PM||||Very NIIIICE!!!||||reg||7
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||12-06-2001||08:09 PM||||Anyone else? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||carpetviper||12-06-2001||09:45 PM||||Does anyone know if CATs are required in VA?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000005||kempo||12-06-2001||10:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by carpetviper:<BR><B>Does anyone know if CATs are required in VA?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Catalytic Converters are in fact a Virginia state Requirement.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/springme.jpg">     <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000006||stingant0||12-06-2001||11:12 PM||||i have the oclet ehuast with no cat and sprint headers. The echaust has a very bad bend in it i think it goes to 1/14 inch. I have noticed a DECREASE in performance. Get a fuel pressure regulator becuase the computer WILL lean out the feul system. It does sound load though. With the underdrive pulley, headers, exhaust, K&N, short shifter, and only 80k my car sux. I can't even beat my friends stock calvier. I know how to launch btw have the ram clutch (do like this ALOT) know how to shift. The V6 is just not worth it in MY opinion. Thats why im going to do a dohc swap. I can sell you my headers if you want them...they have the ceremic coating...only 2 years old. They were like $550 from the fiero store.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||12-07-2001||08:34 AM||||I have the Ocelot, No Cat, and Fiero Store Sprints. There is a gain, It's about 6HP.<BR>The exhaust I have is even all the way thru.<BR>The sound is louder and has more "rasp" to it giving it a "growl".<P>BTW ~ Mine is a 2.8L V-6 with an auto trans and I have no problem beating stock cavalier's and Z-24 cavalier's.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||12-07-2001||09:22 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kempo:<BR><B> Catalytic Converters are in fact a Virginia state Requirement.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I believe catalytic converters are a federal requirement. It's illegal to remove them, no matter where you live. <BR>However, if there is no emissions testing where the car is registered, you probably won't have any problems. <BR>If I didn't live in the metro Atlanta area, I'd be tempted to yank mine. <P>The Ocelot system is one of the best sounding I've ever heard. Guy in our club has one on a 3.4. <BR>Sounds like a stock Fiero, only on steroids.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||12-07-2001||09:41 AM||||Yes, Catalytic converters are a Federal Law. But most states and even the federal EPA allow exemptions for show cars and race cars.<BR>You cannot get an exemption for a daily driven car. I have an exemption from my state. Every 2 years I need to provide them with a rider from the insurance company as to the vehicle's status.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||12-07-2001||09:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Yes, Catalytic converters are a Federal Law. But most states and even the federal EPA allow exemptions for show cars and race cars.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>True. <BR>Forgot about that "show car, race car"<BR>exemption. <BR>(Some of us are too po' to have a show car.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Thanks! <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000011||Turbo88||12-07-2001||10:49 AM||||*I* personally would spend the money elsewhere. It isn't thatttttttttttttt badddddddddddddd of a price but I wouldn't bother unless you have to replace the exhaust for some other reason. The Sprint headers are just too damn pricy for non-tuned headers! Just my .02||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||12-07-2001||11:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Turbo88:<BR>[B The Sprint headers are just too damn pricy for non-tuned headers! [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Non-Tuned? They are tuned to stagger the exhaust. Although they are not equal length tuned like a full set of headers, they are much better than stock and less expensive than a full set of headers. (Actually all aftermarket headers/exhaust manifolds for the Fiero are expensive)<BR>Also on a stock 2.8L going to a full set of headers you will gain about 6-8hp but you will lose low end torque! The full headers flow very well and work well on turbo/SC/NOS or larger displacement engines like the 3.4L.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||stingant0||12-07-2001||12:31 PM||||Don't waste the money on the oclet, it just is not worth the money. If you want a car that looks nice..go with your fiero. If you want a fast car..go with a TurboII dodge car. For $1000 you can get one and with $500 and some help from Gary Donovan--Easly 250 hp at the WHEELS and about 350 ft lbs of torque at the wheels. 10 second fieros anyone?--10 second K-car---Gary Donovan!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Oreif||12-07-2001||12:47 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stingant0:<BR><B>Don't waste the money on the oclet, it just is not worth the money. If you want a car that looks nice..go with your fiero. If you want a fast car..go with a TurboII dodge car. For $1000 you can get one and with $500 and some help from Gary Donovan--Easly 250 hp at the WHEELS and about 350 ft lbs of torque at the wheels. 10 second fieros anyone?--10 second K-car---Gary Donovan!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Look ma another Troll!!<BR>First, this is a "Fiero Forum" not a K-car forum. For a K-car Forum, go here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.allpar.com/eek/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.allpar.com/eek/</A> <P>Second, 250HP in a K-car won't get you to 10's in the 1/4 mile. Click on the above site and you'll see a 265hp K-car that is 13.5 in the 1/4 with a T-3 turbo. Besides the fact a K-car weighs 3220 lbs, 250HP won't do 10's in a car with 1000lbs less weight. There are many 250hp Fiero's here. In fact one person running a stock 2.8L and NOS has 1/4 mile times in the low 12's and dyno shows over 250hp at the wheels.<P>Finally, As for 10-second Fiero's, I know of at least 2 near me and I know there are more.<P>Over 400Hp with no turbos, superchargers, or NOS! Just good old american horsepower.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Drag1.jpg">  <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Zoom88||12-07-2001||07:12 PM||||I have an ocelot system on my car without the Convertor. I am pleased with it, I have had many comments on how good it sounds.<BR>It really gets attention when you let off the gas after accelerating quickly, has a nice rumble and raps off.<p>[This message has been edited by Zoom88 (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||REDHOTT88||12-07-2001||07:32 PM||||Hey ZOOM that was what I wanted to hear!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'm not so much interested in a change of performance, just, does it work and sound good! (I didn't know if ther were any adjustments to make due to lack of cat/conv.)<P>I'm not changing headers either, so I don't care about them at this point.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||stingant0||12-07-2001||08:36 PM||||Oreif first I'm talking about the 2.8 you have another engine so shut up. Can you get into 10's with a 2.8 i dont think so. second go here <A HREF="http://www.thedodgegarage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thedodgegarage.com/</A>  here is a 10 second k-car. dont mess with dodges thats what i have learned. I have a friend that has put no more then $500 in his $1500 daytona and it will run a 13.6 . So dont tell me to go to that wanta be dodge sit. go here and learn about 12.6 caravan. Not that gay site you gave me. The fiero should have stuck with the 2.5 with a turbo not the pos 2.8. So again shut up because you have a hybrid anyway!||||reg||1
Z||000018||Dumba$$||12-07-2001||09:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stingant0:<BR><B>Oreif first I'm talking about the 2.8 you have another engine so shut up. Can you get into 10's with a 2.8 i dont think so. second go here <A HREF="http://www.thedodgegarage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thedodgegarage.com/</A>  here is a 10 second k-car. dont mess with dodges thats what i have learned. I have a friend that has put no more then $500 in his $1500 daytona and it will run a 13.6 . So dont tell me to go to that wanta be dodge sit. go here and learn about 12.6 caravan. Not that gay site you gave me. The fiero should have stuck with the 2.5 with a turbo not the pos 2.8. So again shut up because you have a hybrid anyway!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>hey man i dont want to sound like a dick or anything butt i think oreif has a little more pull here on this forum than you do so can i be the first one to tell you to shut the hell up and go to your back to your farrie dodge site<BR>i agree with oreif  250 hp will not get you 10's<P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>4.9 caddy engine for sale 30,000 miles complete with bubba joes mounts!!  $750||||reg||1
Z||000019||Oreif||12-07-2001||09:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stingant0:<BR><B>Oreif first I'm talking about the 2.8 you have another engine so shut up. Can you get into 10's with a 2.8 i dont think so. second go here <A HREF="http://www.thedodgegarage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thedodgegarage.com/</A>  here is a 10 second k-car. dont mess with dodges thats what i have learned. I have a friend that has put no more then $500 in his $1500 daytona and it will run a 13.6 . So dont tell me to go to that wanta be dodge sit. go here and learn about 12.6 caravan. Not that gay site you gave me. The fiero should have stuck with the 2.5 with a turbo not the pos 2.8. So again shut up because you have a hybrid anyway!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My car isn't a "hybrid", It has a 2.8L. The picture I posted was to a 10 second Fiero since YOU wanted to see one. <BR>The K-car you talk about isn't 250HP it has more. Next the car was set-up for drag strip use only. The inside was gutted and all excess weight removed. Yes it is cool what he did to his K-car and we've seen the van before. If all you care about is going down the 1/4 mile, I can post a link that a guy went 1/4 mile in 9.86 seconds in a normally aspirated Fiero using an SD4 engine. Yes it was built to drag race and the 2.7L SD4 put out 550HP. No turbos, no supercharger, and no NOS. This was all done in 1985! <P>BTW ~ Here is some free advice, We don't care about K-cars or Dodge's, We are here to improve our Fiero's. If this is hard for you to understand then I suggest you "Troll" somewhere else. If you can't control your "attitude" then I suggest you "Shut Up"!<P>||||reg||13
Z||000020||stingant0||12-07-2001||11:07 PM||||Hey guys sorry about that out burst I had a VERY bad week. Finals coming up and lots of papers. I didn't mean that that car was 250 that is what my friend has at the wheels. He only spent $500. Sorry I'm so anti 2.8. I've spent so much time just fixing odd ball things on it that I'm just fed up with it.(80k) Back when I had my automatic, it ran 8.2 everytime, I ALMOST got beat by a PREVIA (Yes the midengine minivan with a soccermom driving it). That was why I wanted a stick. Then when my stick can't beat a stock z24 automatic, well get the point. So again I appologize for the outburst. ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Oreif||12-08-2001||01:46 AM||||Apology accepted, and I'm sorry for back lashing you. It's just lately we've been getting a few "trolls" thru here saying their car is better. <BR>I actually thought you didn't even own a Fiero until later when I saw your posts on the 3.4L stuff. I hope your 3.4 swap goes well. If you have any questions about the actual install, Bob Steiger at Twin Lakes Fiero has done a few of the TDC 3.4L swaps. He may be able to assist you with the mounting logistics if you need them. I am not sure who else has done the swap.||||reg||1
Z||000022||Turbo88||12-08-2001||11:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B> Non-Tuned? They are tuned to stagger the exhaust. Although they are not equal length tuned like a full set of headers, they are much better than stock and less expensive than a full set of headers. (Actually all aftermarket headers/exhaust manifolds for the Fiero are expensive)<BR>Also on a stock 2.8L going to a full set of headers you will gain about 6-8hp but you will lose low end torque! The full headers flow very well and work well on turbo/SC/NOS or larger displacement engines like the 3.4L.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually they aren't tuned. I don't understand what you mean by tuned to stagger the exhaust? What is staggering the exhaust? Maybe for some cylinders to be more for lowend and some for highend? But wouldn't that cause unneeded stress on the rotating assembly because each cylinder isn't matching the others +- a few percent? Those headers don't scavange at all which is the primary point to having headers. Also you can tune your headers to help at the lowend or the high end by adjusting the length of the primaries and the diameter of the collectors. Before I would spend over 500 bucks on a set of better flowing manifolds, I would have a good exhaust shop custom fabricate you a set of headers built and tuned for your engine..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000023||avengador1||12-08-2001||07:58 PM||||But how much would that custom header set cost you? And would they be ceramic coated inside and out?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
